# Machine-readable citation metadata for PointCloudLabeler.
# Spec: https://citation-file-format.github.io/
# Validate: https://cffconvert.readthedocs.io/

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PointCloudLabeler in published work, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "PointCloudLabeler — Tree segmentation and forest inventory from terrestrial and mobile laser scans"
abstract: >-
  An out-of-core, octree-streaming point-cloud editor for forestry
  research. PointCloudLabeler turns raw terrestrial and mobile laser scans into
  traceable per-tree measurements — height, DBH, stem taper, basal
  area, crown metrics, biomass and carbon — with end-to-end
  uncertainty propagation and an occlusion-aware confidence figure
  on every quantity. Implements the Raumonen (2013) TreeQSM
  algorithm with overlapping-ball cover sets, trunk segmentation,
  branch hierarchy and iterative cylinder LSQ fitting.

